// Save as API-Testing-PT.bambda -> Repeater Tab -> Custom Action
// *** ADVANCED & COMPREHENSIVE API SECURITY TESTING FRAMEWORK ***
// Fully automated with 1000+ attack vectors organized for easy maintenance
// All requests are sent directly without creating new tabs
// Results available in Burp Organizer tab with detailed logging
// Supports: JSON, XML, Raw Body, Form Data, URL Parameters, GraphQL
// Authentication: Cookies, Header Tokens (Bearer, API Keys, JWT, OAuth, Basic)
// ============================================================
//
// ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
// │  PART 1: PARAMETER-BASED TESTS                          │
// │  (Executed for EACH parameter found in the request)     │
// └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
//
// Category 1: Input Fuzzing
//   1a. Numeric Fuzzing
//   1b. String Fuzzing
//
// Category 2: Injection Attacks
//   2a. SQL Injection (Time-based, Boolean, Error-based, Union, Stacked)
//   2b. OS Command Injection
//   2c. LDAP Injection
//   2d. XPath Injection
//   2e. Code Injection (PHP, Python, JavaScript, Java)
//   2f. SSRF (Server-Side Request Forgery + Blind SSRF)
//   2g. SSTI (Server-Side Template Injection)
//   2h. Expression Language Injection (SpEL, OGNL, MVEL, EL)
//   2i. Server-Side JavaScript Injection (Node.js)
//
// Category 3: Authorization & Access Control
//   3a. IDOR (Insecure Direct Object References + Advanced Enumeration)
//
// Category 4: Input Validation & Encoding
//   4a. XSS (Cross-Site Scripting)
//   4b. Parameter Pollution
//   4c. JSON Injection
//   4d. NoSQL Injection
//   4e. XXE (XML External Entity)
//   4f. Path Traversal / LFI to RCE
//   4g. Deserialization Attacks
//   4h. CRLF Injection
//   4i. Mass Assignment
//   4j. Prototype Pollution
//   4k. File Upload Bypass
//   4l. Business Logic
//   4m. Unicode Normalization
//   4n. HTML Injection
//   4o. CSV Injection
//   4p. SMTP Header Injection
//
// ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
// │  PART 2: PER-REQUEST TESTS                              │
// │  (Executed ONCE per request - headers/methods/global)   │
// └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
//
// Category 5: Authentication & Session Management
//   5a. Token Tampering
//   5b. JWT Attacks (Algorithm Confusion, JKU/X5U)
//   5c. Session Security
//   5d. 2FA/MFA Bypass
//   5e. OAuth/OIDC Attacks
//
// Category 6: Authorization & Privilege Escalation
//   6a. Privilege Escalation Headers
//
// Category 7: HTTP Protocol & Methods
//   7a. HTTP Method Testing
//   7b. HTTP Verb Tampering
//   7c. URL Manipulation
//
// Category 8: Content Type & Headers
//   8a. Content-Type Bypass
//   8b. CORS Misconfiguration (Advanced)
//   8c. Host Header Injection
//   8d. Cache Poisoning (Unkeyed Headers)
//   8e. Log Injection / Log Forging
//
// Category 9: Security Headers & Configuration
//   9a. Security Headers Analysis
//   9b. Sensitive Data Exposure
//   9c. Cookie Security
//   9d. WebSocket Security
//
// Category 10: Advanced Attacks
//   10a. GraphQL Testing
//   10b. HTTP Request Smuggling
//   10c. Race Conditions (TOCTOU)
//
// ============================================================
// TOTAL: 50+ Vulnerability Categories | 1500+ Payloads
// ============================================================

